## Context Efficiency

**File Operations**: check before reading (Grep first), use `offset`/`limit` for large files, trust writes (no re-reads), spawn agents for multi-file ops (cap at 3 parallel editors per shared tree).

{{#if_module_active lean_ctx}}
**Lean-ctx Bash compression — allow-listed, lossless**: the per-project PreToolUse hook `.claude/hooks/lean-ctx-rewrite.sh` (Windows: `lean-ctx-rewrite.ps1`) compresses ONLY the commands on the one committed allow-list `.claude/hooks/_lib/lean-ctx-allowlist.txt` — package installs, image pulls, downloads, and test/build runners. Everything else runs RAW: loops, pipes, chains, redirects, command substitution, `git`, unknown commands, and anything carrying a credential. When no `lean-ctx` binary is found (PATH, or the probed candidates `~/.cargo/bin`, `~/.local/bin`, `/usr/local/bin`, `/usr/bin`, the Homebrew prefixes), the hook is a graceful no-op and all output is raw.

**Compressed output is never lossy — read the pointer, don't re-run.** Every compressed run tees its FULL raw output to `<project>/.claude/state/lean-ctx-tee/<timestamp>.log` and the compressed output ends with one pointer line. Raw output can carry credentials even when the command text doesn't, so the tee dir is mode 0700 and its files 0600 on POSIX (on Windows the dir and every tee file get an owner-only ACL — inheritance disabled, current user FullControl — and the hook skips compression, passing output through raw, if it cannot make them private); the whole `.claude/` tree is git-excluded at bundle add/update, and `.claude/state/` is transient to the code graph:

```
[lean-ctx-tee] 204 raw lines -> 26 shown; full output: /abs/path/.claude/state/lean-ctx-tee/<ts>.log (kept 168h)
```

When you need a line the compression dropped, **read that file** (it holds every warning, error body and progress line verbatim) — never re-run the command. The tee files self-clean after a TTL (default 168 h; set `VCO_LEAN_CTX_TEE_TTL_HOURS` in `.claude/env`, `0` = keep forever).

**Bypass** (rare — the pointer already gives you the full output; use these only when you want raw *inline*):

| Scope | Mechanism | When to use |
|---|---|---|
| Per-call | `lean-ctx bypass "<cmd>"` or `lean-ctx -c --raw "<cmd>"` | See raw output inline for ONE command. The hook steps aside for any command starting with `lean-ctx` — no double-wrap. |
| Per-project | `VCO_LEAN_CTX_DEFAULT=off` in `.claude/env` | Turn compression off for this project (default `on`). Launcher: project → Hooks tab → "Bash output compression". |
| Global | `export VCT_DISABLE_HOOKS=1` | Disables ALL VCO hooks for the shell, not just lean-ctx — for debugging hook interactions only. |

Two conservative arms keep output lossless either way: when the state dir can't be created the command runs raw and uncompressed inline (no tee, no pointer — nothing was dropped); when the raw output exceeds 32 MiB only the pointer is printed and the full output is read from the tee file.
{{/if_module_active}}

