## Update flow

Two distinct "update" actions live in the launcher:

- **Update orchestrator** (Settings → Updates) — refreshes the orchestrator clone itself (the global venv, bundled hooks/MCP servers, the templates folder, the launcher and hub binaries). Stops the detached `vct-hub` before the update so the binary swap isn't blocked on Windows, then restarts it and the launcher.
- **Update bundle** (per-project Settings page → "Update bundle" button; the Projects page's "⟳ Update all" button runs it on every registered project) — propagates newly-shipped orchestrator files to an existing user project. The orchestrator root is skipped by ⟳ Update all when its bundle is already current — the per-project Settings page's Update bundle always runs. CLI equivalent: `'{{VENV_PYTHON}}' -m vco_lib.project_init install-bundle --folder <project> --orchestrator-root '{{ORCHESTRATOR_ROOT}}' --update`.

The "Update bundle" path is manifest-driven via `<project>/.claude/.vco-manifest.json`:
- New shipped file → created in the project.
- Installed file matches the manifest's prior-shipped hash (= untouched since install) → overwritten with the new shipped version.
- Installed file differs from the manifest's prior-shipped hash (= locally modified) → **adopted**: the current bytes are backed up to `<project>/.claude/backups/bundle-adoptions/<timestamp>/<path>`, then the shipped version is written. Only if that backup cannot be written is the file left alone and a `bundle_user_modified_preserved` deferral entry written to `<project>/.claude/context/UPDATE_DEFERRED.md`. That entry names the failed backup write and quotes its error per file, and its remedies are ordered: fix the backup destination (free space, write permission, no symlink under `.claude/backups/`) and re-run the ORDINARY update — which adopts the files, captures the backups and clears the entry by itself — then dismiss, then diff per file, and only last `--force`, which writes the shipped version with NO backup on the very machine whose backup writes just failed.
- `knowledge/**` is the exception: a modified KG node is the user's data and is **always preserved** — on the normal path and under `--force` alike.
- Schema drift detected (Weaviate target schema differs from on-disk) → `schema_migration_required` deferral entry; the destructive migration is NOT auto-applied. Requires explicit consent via `python -m vco_lib.project_init migrate-collections --name <project>`.

The launcher toast summarises the counts. Soft-fail throughout: subprocess errors flow through warnings, never block.

