## Moving a project to a different folder

The step-by-step protocol ships in every project's own `CLAUDE.md` (rendered
from `templates/CLAUDE.md.template`, section "Moving this project to a
different folder"). Treat that as the single source of truth and do not fork a
second copy here — its steps already cover the traps: project identity resolves
from the registered launcher row and the live bindings, never from the folder
basename (a deferral ledger written by an older VCO version can still carry a
command built on the old, wrong identity, so re-verify before running any
collection drop), `.mcp.json` taking precedence over `.claude/settings.json`,
and which DB columns are operational (rewrite) versus historical (leave
alone). A correct move never re-embeds anything — Weaviate object metadata
stores relative paths — so if you find yourself re-embedding, stop and
re-check.

